hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"276","Yahya bin Hakim narrated, Omar bin Ali narrated, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated, he said: I heard Fatima bint Al-Mundhir speaking, on the authority of her grandmother, Asma The daughter of Abu Bakr, that she heard a woman asking the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: If one of us becomes pure, what will she do with her clothes? What was she wearing? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If she sees something in it, let her scratch it, then sprinkle some water on it, and sprinkle water throughout the garment and pray.” “In it.” On the authority of Yahya bin Hakim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, like this, and he said: And he said: “If you see blood on it, wipe it off, then Cover it with water, then sprinkle the rest of it, then pray in it.”"
